From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: irisrun <irisrun@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:54:08 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 26/37] Add menus, context menus and long presses on Linux

Menu opens a panel of its items next to its label, below it when there is
room, each item a row with its icon at the trailing edge; a tap outside
closes it, and a nested menu opens another panel. contextMenu opens one
on a long press, in a scroll view too, without tapping the view. A menu
picker opens a menu of its options with the selected one checked.

LongPressGesture ends once the finger has been down long enough, and
onLongPressGesture runs its action then. The stdout app gets a hold
command for it.
